import random
n = 100000
c = 0
for i in range(n):
  t = random.randint(1,6)
  g = random.randint(1,6)


  if t + g == 7:
    c += 1
print((c/n)*100)

Just a way to turn probability into computational experiment
The most important thing here is the sampling error decreases roughly to 1/sqrt(n)

100 times as many simulations generally reduces sampling error by about a factor of 10
